{
  "content": "<h1><span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"PayslipEarningsItems\">Payslip Earnings Items</span></h1><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Earnings Employee Item On Payment Payments Payslip PayslipEarningsItem PayslipEarningsItems Payslips Rent Type\">Payslip earnings items define the different types of payments that can be included on employee payslips.</p><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"And Earnings Is On Other Type\">Set up standard earnings categories such as regular wages, overtime pay, bonuses, commissions, allowances, and other compensation types.</p><h2 translate=\"true\" keywords=\"View\">Overview</h2><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"And Create Earnings Is Item On Payslip Payslips Port Rent Select Type\">Each earnings item you create becomes available for selection when preparing payslips. This ensures consistency in how different types of earnings are recorded and reported.</p><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Account Accounts Automatic ChartOfAccounts Count Earnings ExpenseAccount Item To ToDate\">Earnings items are linked to expense accounts in your chart of accounts, allowing automatic posting of wage costs to the correct accounts.</p><h2 translate=\"true\" keywords=\"\">Getting Started</h2><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Create Earnings Item NewPayslip NewPayslipItem On Payslip To ToDate\">To create a new earnings item, click the <strong>New Payslip Item</strong> button. You can create as many earnings items as needed to match your payroll structure.</p><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"And Earnings Is Item On Rate Sales\">Common earnings items include basic salary, overtime rates, performance bonuses, sales commissions, housing allowances, and travel allowances.</p><details><summary><span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"Name\">Name</span></summary><div><div class=\"my-4\"><div class=\"border rounded p-0.5 pointer-events-none text-sm w-max\"><div class=\"grid grid-cols-[1.25rem_auto_1.25rem] bg-neutral-200 gap-[1px]\"><div class=\"bg-neutral-100 h-2\"></div><div class=\"bg-neutral-100 h-2\"></div><div class=\"bg-neutral-100 h-2\"></div><div class=\"bg-neutral-100 border-t border-t-white\"></div><div class=\"bg-neutral-100 font-bold text-neutral-500 text-shadow px-4 py-2 border-t border-t-white\"><span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"Name\">Name</span></div><div class=\"bg-neutral-100 border-t border-t-white\"></div><div class=\"bg-neutral-50 border-t border-white h-2\"></div><div class=\"bg-neutral-50 border-t border-white h-2\"></div><div class=\"bg-neutral-50 border-t border-white h-2\"></div></div></div></div><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Earnings Item Name On Payslip Payslips\">The name of the earnings item that will appear on payslips.</p><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Is On\">Examples include basic salary, overtime pay, bonuses, commissions, or allowances.</p><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"And Employee Employees Name On Payslip Payslips\">Choose descriptive names that employees will easily understand on their payslips.</p></div></details><details><summary><span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"ExpenseAccount\">Expense account</span></summary><div><div class=\"my-4\"><div class=\"border rounded p-0.5 pointer-events-none text-sm w-max\"><div class=\"grid grid-cols-[1.25rem_auto_1.25rem] bg-neutral-200 gap-[1px]\"><div class=\"bg-neutral-100 h-2\"></div><div class=\"bg-neutral-100 h-2\"></div><div class=\"bg-neutral-100 h-2\"></div><div class=\"bg-neutral-100 border-t border-t-white\"></div><div class=\"bg-neutral-100 font-bold text-neutral-500 text-shadow px-4 py-2 border-t border-t-white\"><span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"ExpenseAccount\">Expense account</span></div><div class=\"bg-neutral-100 border-t border-t-white\"></div><div class=\"bg-neutral-50 border-t border-white h-2\"></div><div class=\"bg-neutral-50 border-t border-white h-2\"></div><div class=\"bg-neutral-50 border-t border-white h-2\"></div></div></div></div><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Account Count Earnings ExpenseAccount HasWhere Is Item\">The expense account where this earnings item will be posted.</p><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Account And Count ExpenseAccount Is Profit ProfitAndLossStatement Statement\">This is typically a wages or salaries expense account in your <em>profit and loss statement</em>.</p><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Account Count Earnings Is Select Suspense To ToDate\">If no account is selected, earnings will be posted to the <em>suspense account</em>.</p></div></details><details><summary><span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"ReportingCategory\">Reporting Category</span></summary><div><div class=\"my-4\"><div class=\"border rounded p-0.5 pointer-events-none text-sm w-max\"><div class=\"grid grid-cols-[1.25rem_auto_1.25rem] bg-neutral-200 gap-[1px]\"><div class=\"bg-neutral-100 h-2\"></div><div class=\"bg-neutral-100 h-2\"></div><div class=\"bg-neutral-100 h-2\"></div><div class=\"bg-neutral-100 border-t border-t-white\"></div><div class=\"bg-neutral-100 font-bold text-neutral-500 text-shadow px-4 py-2 border-t border-t-white\"><span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"ReportingCategory\">Reporting Category</span></div><div class=\"bg-neutral-100 border-t border-t-white\"></div><div class=\"bg-neutral-50 border-t border-white h-2\"></div><div class=\"bg-neutral-50 border-t border-white h-2\"></div><div class=\"bg-neutral-50 border-t border-white h-2\"></div></div></div></div><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Earnings Group Item Port ReportingCategory Reports\">The reporting category for grouping earnings items in reports.</p><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Business By On Other Port ReportingCategories To ToDate Type\">Use reporting categories to analyze payroll costs by type, department, or any other classification relevant to your business.</p></div></details>",
  "key": "payslip-earnings-items"
